  "baseline_identity": {
    "IQL": "Discrete-action adaptation: twin Q heads, upper-expectile V regression, advantage-weighted categorical policy extraction, cap 100; update V, actor, Q, targets. Uses target Q for V/actor as in the official implementation.",
    "CQL": "Discrete SAC-CQL: twin Q heads, exact supported-action soft Bellman expectation, logsumexp(Q)-Q(data) conservative penalty, categorical maximum-entropy actor; original scalar-Q architecture. Not QR-DQN CQL.",
    "PS": "Prioritized Sweeping + native actor: optimal (max-action) graph Bellman backups, not current-policy evaluation. Replay records seed a priority queue; changed action values enqueue predecessor pairs. Same supplied Qold initializes the sparse value table; supported dependencies are traversed without depth truncation. Budgets count performed scalar backups, transition reads reported separately.",
    "TD_PER_DISCOR_EXTRA_TD": "Native actor with gain 1 or 8; complete AWAC weight detached. PER alpha .4, importance beta .4->1; DisCor error lr1e-4, initial temperature10, target/temperature EMA .005; Extra TD makes 8 critic batches per actor update."
  },
  "initialization": "Common initial actor/critic state is checked bitwise. IQL/CQL retain existing twin heads where available; otherwise clone the available initial head and optimizer. IQL V starts at the initial actor expectation of the initial twin-min critic plus a zero residual; all added networks and optimizers are in complete checkpoints.",
